acquisition as an indirect benefit of using LLM-assistants. Although the main goal is to speed up the development
process, 69% of participants report that the employed code translation LLM-assistant enhanced their learning (e.g.,
taught them new aspects of Python) [PS2].
Further evidence is provided by Khojah et al. [PS7], who analyze developer interactions with ChatGPT. Their findings
show that expert consultation is the most common use case, accounting for 62% of the analyzed conversations [PS7].
Participants from the same study further highlight such benefits, where 75% of survey respondents report ChatGPT
as a helpful learning tool [PS7]. LLM-assistants are also found to lower the barrier of learning new frameworks,
enabling developers to start immediately rather than navigating extensive tutorials [PS15, PS34]. Additionally, one
study involving 14 experts in SE finds that enhancing learning and teaching is the most probable future scenario with
LLM-assistants [PS31].
6.1.5 Support code-adjacent tasks.The benefits of LLM-assistants extend beyond coding tasks to support code-related
activities. For instance, studies highlight the use of LLM-assistants for ideation [PS36] by exploring different solutions
options, requirements specifications [PS28, PS36] including functional and non-functional requirements, documen-
tation [PS5, PS9, PS11, PS36] such as in-code documentation and API documentation, and quality assurance [PS11,
PS24]. Developers also use LLM tools for composing emails, generating meeting minutes, and creating onboarding
documentation [PS34]. AI assisted teams document significantly more GitHub issues and coordinate more effectively
through improved information externalization [PS4].
6.1.6 Reduce task initiation overhead.A common reported benefit across primary studies is the use of LLM-assistants
to support task or project initiation [PS2, PS8, PS11, PS21, PS24, PS33, PS34]. Several studies note that developers rely
on these tools as astarting pointfor a project or task [PS2, PS33], effectively lowering the entry barrier [PS24]. These
tools help developers build momentum by reducing the time and cognitive effort required during the early stages of a
project. For example, developers highlight how LLM-assistants can accelerate the development of proof-of-concept
applications by generating multiple candidate implementations for the same task [PS11] generating an initial structure
when starting new topics [PS21].

